response:
 When a cube is rolled, each of its 6 faces has an equal chance of being on top. Here, the probability that a particular face on top must be the number of favorable outcomes over the number of possible outcomes. 
The number of blue faces = {4}
Number of red faces = {2}
Total faces = {4+2=6}
Probability of rolling a blue face on top = $$ \frac{total_no\; of\; favorable\; outcomes}{total\; number\; of\; outcomes}$$
$$= \frac{6}{6}= 1$$
So, the probability = $$\frac{4}{6}= \frac{2}{3}$$</answer>
